<p><strong>What this does NOT change:</strong> the volume dependency. Every lever above lowers the bar; only the channels (clinic-declined referrals at zero CAC, SEO, communities) clear it. The March checkpoint in §8 remains the decision that matters.</p>
<h2>8c. The solo-founder cash model (the operator&rsquo;s actual position)</h2>
<p>Sections 7–8b model <em>staffed</em> scenarios from the implementation plan&rsquo;s team assumptions. The operating reality is <strong>one founder, home-based, no payroll</strong> — which converts the model from a P&amp;L question into a cash-flow question, and changes the answer dramatically:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fixed cash ≈ $1,100/month</strong> (hosting budgeted ~$150 — provisioned actual ~$88, see §5b; E&amp;O ~$250, counsel pay-as-you-go ~$200, $500 marketing floor). No salaries, no office.</li>
<li><strong>Cash contribution ≈ $278/case</strong> — QA is founder time (sweat equity, not cash), so cash COGS is ~$31 (OCR + LLM + storage + Stripe + expected refunds).</li>
<li><strong>Cash break-even: ~4 cases/month.</strong></li>
</ul>
